---
// privacy.astro — the public Privacy Policy for the Gurbani Soul iOS app (org.sggs.app) and this site.
// Linked from the App Store listing (Privacy Policy URL) and from /support. Every statement
// here is checked against the code: PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy, Info.plist, SolarLocation.swift,
// CrashMonitor.swift, SpotlightIndex.swift, WidgetShared.swift, NitnemReminders.swift,
// NitnemProgress.swift, ReadingActivityController.swift, and the frontend scripts
// (components/Analytics.astro loads Vercel Web Analytics on the gurbanisoul.com marketing pages only).
// Keep it true before you keep it short. Rendered in the marketing shell (LegalPage) since v1.3.5;
// the path /privacy is frozen (App Store Connect + the app's AppLinks).
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
const updated = "23 September 2026";
// The launch-notice sign-up (Newsletter.astro) renders only when this build-time env var is set;
// the disclosure below follows it, so the policy never describes a form the site does not show.
const newsletterOn = !!import.meta.env.PUBLIC_NEWSLETTER_FORM_URL;
const desc = "The Gurbani Soul app collects nothing: no accounts, no network connections, no analytics. Exactly what stays on your device, and what this website does.";
const toc = [
  { id: "short-version", label: "The short version" },
  { id: "the-app", label: "The app" },
  { id: "this-website", label: "This website" },
  { id: "children", label: "Children" },
  { id: "your-data", label: "Your data, your control" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact" },
];
---
<Marketing title="Privacy Policy — Gurbani Soul" description={desc} path="/privacy">
  <LegalPage
    eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
    title="The app collects nothing. Here is exactly what that means."
    id="v-privacy"
    toc={toc}
    updated={updated}
  >
    <section id="short-version">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p class="legal-scope">Applies to the <strong>Gurbani Soul</strong> app for iPhone and iPad (bundle <code>org.sggs.app</code>, including its widgets and Live Activity) and to this website.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts. Nothing to sign up for, nothing to log in to.</li>
        <li>The app makes <strong>no network connections</strong>. It works fully in Airplane Mode.</li>
        <li>No analytics, no advertising, no tracking, no third-party SDKs in the app. This website counts page views anonymously, without cookies; see <a href="#this-website">This website</a>.</li>
        <li>Everything you do in the app (saved verses, settings, reading position, Nitnem progress and reminders) stays on your device.</li>
        <li>Location is optional, used only on your device, and never transmitted.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="the-app">
      <h2>The app</h2>
      <p>The app bundles the complete text of Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji, plus the Nitnem banis as a separate, labelled layer, and searches it locally. It never sends a request to any server, so we cannot see what you read, search for or save. Specifically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Saved verses</strong> are stored in the app's own database on your device. If you save a verse, it is also added to your device's Spotlight index so you can find it from the Home Screen search; unsaving removes it. Spotlight data stays on your device.</li>
        <li><strong>Settings</strong> (accent colour, transliteration, traditional rendering, last Ang read) are stored in the app's local preferences.</li>
        <li><strong>Nitnem</strong> progress (where you are in each bani, which days you completed it, your own sets and journey) is stored in small files in the app's own App Group container on your device, so the Nitnem widget can show it. It is never transmitted.</li>
        <li><strong>Reminders</strong> are optional local notifications. The app asks for notification permission only when you turn a reminder on, schedules them on your device at the times you choose, and uses no push service: no notification ever comes from a server, and no device token is created or sent anywhere.</li>
        <li><strong>Live Activity</strong> is optional and off by default. When you turn it on, a reading session shows its progress on your Lock Screen and in the Dynamic Island. It is driven entirely on your device (no push updates) and never shows a verse.</li>
        <li><strong>Widgets</strong> read a small snapshot the app writes into its own App Group container on your device: the raag watch, a Hukam verse with its Ang, today's Nitnem progress, and — if you use solar mode — your clock-mode choice and the same ~1 km rounded coordinates. Nothing leaves the device.</li>
        <li><strong>Location</strong> is used only by the Raag Clock's optional solar mode to compute local sunrise and sunset. It is requested only when you turn that mode on. The fix is rounded to two decimal places (about 1 km) before it is stored in the app's own App Group container — shared only with the app's widgets on the same device — and the raw position is never kept. You can enter a location manually instead, or deny the permission; the clock still works.</li>
        <li><strong>Integrity checks</strong> read the bundled scripture database's size and modification date to decide whether its checksum needs re-verifying. This is why the app's privacy manifest declares the "file timestamp" and "user defaults" API reasons. Nothing is displayed or transmitted.</li>
        <li><strong>Diagnostics</strong>: if the app ever crashes or hangs, iOS may hand it a diagnostic report. The app writes that report to its own local folder; it is never uploaded. You can see how many there are, share them via the system share sheet to a destination you choose, or delete them under More → About &amp; credits → Integrity — nothing leaves the device unless you send it. Separately, Apple may share crash reports with us through App Store Connect <em>only</em> if you have enabled "Share with App Developers" in your iOS Privacy &amp; Security → Analytics settings. Those reports are governed by Apple's privacy policy and contain no account or identity information.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Because the app collects no data, its App Store privacy label is <strong>"Data Not Collected"</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="this-website">
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The site is static, carries no advertising, and sets no cookies.</li>
        <li>The Gurbani Soul pages (the home page, Features, The watch, Learn, Support and this policy) count page views with <strong>Vercel Web Analytics</strong>, and only when served from gurbanisoul.com. It uses no cookies and does not follow you across other sites. It records the page, the referring site, and your country, browser, operating system and device type as anonymous totals; visitors are counted with a short-lived hash that is discarded after a day. We do not build profiles from it or share it.</li>
        <li>The Knowledge Base pages (search, reader and the study tools) load no analytics.</li>
        {newsletterOn && <li>If you ask to be told when the app is on the App Store, the email address you type is sent to <strong>Buttondown</strong>, which sends that one email. Nothing else is sent with it, and you can unsubscribe from the email itself.</li>}
        <li>Your browser's local storage holds your theme choice, the traditional-rendering toggle, and any verses you pin to the Study Trail. This lives in your browser only; clearing site data removes it.</li>
        <li>Searches and page requests are answered by our API. The hosting providers we use (Vercel for the site, Render for the API) keep standard server logs — IP address, user agent, request path and time — for security and operations, under their own retention rules. We do not add tracking to those logs, do not build profiles from them, and do not share them.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="children">
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The app is rated 4+ and collects no personal information from anyone, of any age.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-data">
      <h2>Your data, your control</h2>
      <p>We hold no data about you, so there is nothing for us to export, correct or delete. Everything the app stores is on your device: deleting the app removes it. Everything the site stores is in your browser: clearing site data removes it.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy ever changes, the date at the top changes with it and the new text is published here before it takes effect. The app will not start collecting data without a new version, a new policy, and a new App Store privacy label.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:support@gurbanisoul.com">support@gurbanisoul.com</a>. For help with the app, see <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </LegalPage>

  <style>
    .legal-scope { color: var(--ink-soft); }
    :global(.legal code) { font-size: .85em; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--paper-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
    :global(.legal li) { margin: 6px 0; }
  </style>
</Marketing>
